# Copy to .env.local and fill in from Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys.
#
# Both values are NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which means Next inlines them into the
# JavaScript bundle served to the browser. They are NOT secrets, and cannot be:
# the browser has to hold them to talk to Supabase at all. What protects your
# data is row-level security, which scopes every query to the signed-in user.
#
# Because of that, these belong in Vercel's environment variables and — if you
# want CI to build against the real project — GitHub Actions *variables*, not
# Actions *secrets*. A secret would be pointlessly redacted in build logs while
# still shipping in the bundle. See SETUP.md.
#
# NEVER put the service-role / secret key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable or in this
# file. It bypasses row-level security entirely, and anything here reaches the
# browser.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-OR-PUBLISHABLE-KEY
